  "established_findings": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "kind": "DECOMPOSITION_DECISION",
      "classification": "LEAF_EXECUTABLE",
      "finding": "The objective is atomic enough for one leaf process; no decomposition is warranted."
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "kind": "CONTRACT_REQUIREMENT",
      "finding": "A terminal claim requires at least two experiment/result cycles, rejection of at least one competing hypothesis, and addressing O1."
    },
    {
      "id": "L1",
      "kind": "EXPERIMENT_INTERPRETATION",
      "finding": "E_restore_timeout restored the prior 12-second client timeout and produced p95_latency_ms=5100 with timeout_failure_rate=0.01. Requests can therefore complete beyond the former ~5.0-second failure boundary when that timeout is removed, supporting H_timeout_config."
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "kind": "EXPERIMENT_INTERPRETATION",
      "finding": "E_double_cpu doubled CPU and produced p95_latency_ms=5000 with timeout_failure_rate=0.39. The failure boundary remained at about 5.0 seconds and the timeout failure rate remained high, so added CPU did not remove the deadline failures. This rejects H_cpu as the leading explanation and, together with L1, leaves H_timeout_config as the supported explanation."
    },
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "kind": "INDEPENDENT_CRITIQUE",
      "finding": "Independent review approves L1 and L2 and their experiment-result bindings. E_restore_timeout changes the client-timeout intervention while holding load/infrastructure fixed and reduces timeout_failure_rate to 0.01 while allowing p95_latency_ms=5100, directly explaining O1's ~5.0-second cutoff and supporting H_timeout_config. E_double_cpu leaves the 5-second timeout unchanged and yields p95_latency_ms=5000 with timeout_failure_rate=0.39, so added CPU does not remove the cutoff; H_cpu is appropriately rejected. Required synthesis guardrails: explicitly address O1; bind observed_results to the two exact published raw result hashes; reject H_cpu; do not claim H_network was experimentally rejected because no network-bypass result is durable. H_network need not be experimentally rejected by the public worker contract, which requires rejection of at least one competing hypothesis."
    }
  ],
